{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/esengine/DeepSeek-Reasonix/pulls/7777","id":4221640401,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSIatD877oR7R","html_url":"https://github.com/esengine/DeepSeek-Reasonix/pull/7777","diff_url":"https://github.com/esengine/DeepSeek-Reasonix/pull/7777.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/esengine/DeepSeek-Reasonix/pull/7777.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/esengine/DeepSeek-Reasonix/issues/7777","number":7777,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat(long-horizon): OSWorld 2.0 implicit-state retention + navigator wiring","user":{"login":"bfxh","id":243242559,"node_id":"U_kgDODn-WPw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/243242559?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bfxh","html_url":"https://github.com/bfxh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bfxh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bfxh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bfxh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bfxh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bfxh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bfxh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bfxh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bfxh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bfxh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Cache-impact: low - compaction prompt selection and StateTracker/Navigator wiring are gated on long_horizon (false = legacy 7-section prompt, unchanged behavior). No change to cache prefix calculation.\nCache-guard: go test ./internal/agent/ ./internal/navigator/ ./internal/boot/ ./internal/config/\nSystem-prompt-review: N/A - no system_prompt_file modified.\nDocumentation-impact: updated - long_horizon / verification_interval behavior now matches docs/OSWORLD2_ANALYSIS.md (runtime nudge implemented).\n\n## Summary\n\nOSWorld 2.0-informed long-horizon state management for the agent, addressing all 5 blockers from the #7743 review:\n\n1. **Navigator wired into the production tool path (was dead code).** `run_loop` feeds every host-executed tool call through `NavigatorKernel.ObserveToolCall` — advisory mode: the navigator records observations into its state graph, recovers implicit facts, and returns correction advice as Notice events. It **never re-executes tools**, so permission gate / Pre-PostToolUse hooks / evidence recording stay with the agent's own `CallResolver` path. `boot` gates Navigator+StateTracker wiring on `long_horizon`; `agent.New` purifies typed-nil interface values.\n2. **`verification_interval` runtime nudge.** Every N tool-call rounds (long-horizon only) the run loop injects a verification checkpoint message reminding the model to verify goal alignment, re-check hidden-state assumptions, and surface open questions — no longer config-only.\n3. **Real per-call errors reach the StateTracker.** `executeBatch` now returns `errs`; `AfterToolCall` receives the actual error instead of hard-coded nil, so failed calls are recorded as failures and error facts are captured.\n4. **Implicit facts bounded and deduped.** StateTracker dedupes by (source, fact) with later-wins and caps the set at 500 entries; navigator's upsert already deduped by key. Long tasks no longer grow state without bound or re-inject the same facts at every compaction.\n5. **`long_horizon=false` now means what it says.** No StateTracker/Navigator construction, legacy 7-section compaction prompt, no implicit-state injection — the boot diagnostic no longer claims \"7 sections / no implicit-state capture\" while the 10-section prompt runs.\n\nBranch history (11 commits): meta-tool base (5) + long-horizon tuning, StateTracker, Navigator kernel + HERMES adapter, gofmt, CodeQL fix, and this review-fix commit.\n\n## Issues\n\n## Verification\n\n- go build ./... -> ok\n- go test ./internal/navigator/ ./internal/agent/ ./internal/boot/ ./internal/config/ -> all ok (agent 25s incl. new integration test)\n- go test ./internal/... -> all ok except pre-existing Windows symlink-permission failures in internal/repair (environment, unrelated)\n- gofmt clean; git diff --check clean\n- New tests: ObserveToolCall advisory suite (never-executes / failure advice / multi-call tracking), StateTracker dedup+cap+error-recording, summary-prompt switch (7 vs 10 sections), executeBatch err exposure, Run-level integration test (TestRunLoopFeedsNavigatorAndTracker)\n\n## Documentation impact\n\nDocumentation-impact: updated - long_horizon / verification_interval docs (docs/OSWORLD2_ANALYSIS.md) now match the implemented runtime behavior.\n\n## Cache impact\n\nCache-impact: low - compaction prompt selection and state wiring are gated on long_horizon; legacy behavior (long_horizon=false) is byte-identical. No change to cache prefix calculation or invalidation.\nCache-guard: go test ./internal/agent/ ./internal/navigator/ ./internal/boot/ ./internal/config/\nSystem-prompt-review: N/A - no system_prompt_file modified.","created_at":"2026-08-06T14:13:18Z","updated_at":"2026-08-06T14:15:41Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"esengine","id":18465053,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDY1MDUz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18465053?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/esengine","html_url":"https://github.com/esengine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esengine/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esengine/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esengine/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esengine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esengine/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esengine/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esengine/repos","events_url":"https://api.g